<h2>Why net worth beats income</h2>
<p>It is easy to look rich and be broke. A big paycheck spent on big payments leaves you with nothing to show for it. Net worth cuts through the noise. It does not care what you make or what you drive. It only asks one question: after everything you owe, what is actually yours? That is the number the wealthy quietly watch, and it is the one to start watching too.</p>

<h2>How to make it grow</h2>
<p>There are only two levers. Grow the assets side by saving and investing consistently, and shrink the debt side by paying down what you owe. Do both at once and your net worth climbs from both directions. You do not need a windfall. You need a small, steady gap between what you earn and what you spend, pointed at these two jobs, month after month.</p>

<p><em>This is general education, not personal advice, so check with a licensed professional about your situation.</em></p>

